{
  "_readme": [
    "Golden vectors for the canonical identity layer (docs/specs/2026-08-14-unified-db-and-autofetch-design.md §1).",
    "This file is the CONTRACT between the two implementations:",
    "  desktop  src/identity.mjs           — tested by  node tools/identity/test.mjs",
    "  app      data/identity/Identity.kt  — tested by  cd android && ./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest",
    "Both tests read THIS file. Neither has its own copy. If they disagree, the merge is broken.",
    "Add a case here FIRST, then make both sides pass it.",
    "Escapes: \\u0000 is the NULL-cell sentinel, \\u001f is the unit separator.",
    "syncedCols/merge/nextUpdatedAt cover the §3 merge engine (src/merge.mjs and data/sync/MergeEngine.kt). A merge case with \"tiebreak\": true has no fixed expected action: the rule is only that BOTH implementations pick the same side, so each test asserts its own result equals greater-content-hash-wins.",
    "oldSurveyMatch covers §2 (src/old-survey-match.mjs and data/sync/OldSurveyMatcher.kt)."
  ],
